  "slug": "mitochondrial-acid-2d6e",
  "summary": "Five preprints converge on mitochondrial import, dynamics and fatty acid oxidation across muscle, liver, adipose and immune cells.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is that mitochondrial substrate entry and organelle remodeling set tissue metabolic output. Two preprints identify SLC25A35 as the mitochondrial carrier for branched-chain keto acids (BCKAs). One of them also names MCT1 and MCT2 as cellular entry transporters and reports that import limits hepatic BCKA handling, while the other links BCKA uptake to adipocyte lipogenesis and fatty acid metabolism. MTCH2 supports mitochondrial metabolic remodeling, respiration and fatty acid oxidation in muscle satellite cells. Myeloid mDIC deletion shifts adipose macrophages toward an efferocytosis-associated state while preserving mitochondrial respiration. In KPC cachexia mice, muscle OPA1 overexpression or BNIP3 knockdown partly preserved muscle mass and function in a sex-dependent manner. Dual Hadha and Hadhb mRNA delivery restores fatty acid oxidation in a trifunctional protein deficiency model. The new element is the transporter-level account of BCKA import, linking cellular uptake to mitochondrial entry.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
